## Type-Level vs Method-Level Generics

### Type-Level Generic (on struct)
```xiom
pub type Container[T] = { value: T; }

impl Container[T] {
  fn get(self: &Self) -> &T { return &self.value; }
}
```

### Method-Level Generic (on method)
```xiom
impl Container[T] {
  fn map[U](self: &Self, f: fn(&T) -> U) -> Container[U] {
    return Container[U]{ value: f(&self.value) };
  }
}
```

T is from the type, U is from the method — independent!

### Common Patterns
```xiom
impl Option[T] {
  fn map[U](self: &Self, f: fn(&T) -> U) -> Option[U] {
    match self {
      Some(v) => Some(f(v)),
      None => None(),
    }
  }

  fn and_then[U](self: &Self, f: fn(&T) -> Option[U]) -> Option[U] {
    match self {
      Some(v) => f(v),
      None => None(),
    }
  }
}

impl Result[T, E] {
  fn map[U](self: &Self, f: fn(&T) -> U) -> Result[U, E] {
    match self {
      Ok(v) => Ok(f(v)),
      Err(e) => Err(e),
    }
  }

  fn map_err[F](self: &Self, f: fn(&E) -> F) -> Result[T, F] {
    match self {
      Ok(v) => Ok(v),
      Err(e) => Err(f(e)),
    }
  }
}
```

